### Health check
GET http://localhost:8080/api/health


### Get all assets
GET http://localhost:8080/api/assets


### Filter assets by status
GET http://localhost:8080/api/assets?status=AVAILABLE


### Filter assets by category
GET http://localhost:8080/api/assets?category=Laptop


### Filter assets by location
GET http://localhost:8080/api/assets?location=HQ


### Get paged assets
GET http://localhost:8080/api/assets/paged?page=0&size=5


### Get paged assets sorted by name ascending
GET http://localhost:8080/api/assets/paged?page=0&size=5&sortBy=name&direction=asc


### Get paged assets sorted by assetTag descending
GET http://localhost:8080/api/assets/paged?page=0&size=5&sortBy=assetTag&direction=desc


### Create valid asset
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetTag": "CAM-2026-1001",
  "name": "Logitech Webcam",
  "category": "Camera",
  "serialNumber": "SN-CAM-1001",
  "location": "HQ Level 2"
}


### Create duplicate asset tag - should return 409 Conflict
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetTag": "CAM-2026-1001",
  "name": "Duplicate Webcam",
  "category": "Camera",
  "serialNumber": "SN-CAM-2002",
  "location": "HQ Level 2"
}


### Create duplicate serial number - should return 409 Conflict
POST http://localhost:8080/api/assets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetTag": "CAM-2026-3003",
  "name": "Another Webcam",
  "category": "Camera",
  "serialNumber": "SN-CAM-1001",
  "location": "HQ Level 2"
}

### ---------------------------
### TICKET API TESTS (DAY 7)
### ---------------------------

### 1. Get all tickets from MongoDB
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets


### 2. Get one ticket by ID
# IMPORTANT: Run the "Get all tickets" request above first. 
# Look at the JSON response, copy the 24-character "id", and replace YOUR_REAL_TICKET_ID below!
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/YOUR_REAL_TICKET_ID


### 3. Get missing ticket (Should return 404 Not Found)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/000000000000000000000000

### 4. Create a valid ticket (Day 7 Exercise 4)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Cannot access email",
  "description": "User cannot login to company email account.",
  "category": "Email",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "createdBy": "amir@example.com"
}


### 5. Create an invalid ticket (Should return 400 Bad Request)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "",
  "category": "",
  "priority": "",
  "createdBy": ""
}

### Day 8: Get all tickets (No filters)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets

### Day 8: Filter tickets by Status
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets?status=OPEN

### Day 8: Filter tickets by Priority
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets?priority=HIGH

### Day 8: Filter tickets by Category
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets?category=Email

### Day 8 Ex 2: Get paginated tickets (Page 0, Default sorting)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=5

### Day 8 Ex 2: Get paginated tickets (Page 1)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/paged?page=1&size=5

### Day 8 Ex 2: Get paginated tickets (Custom sort: Priority Ascending, size 2)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=2&sortBy=priority&direction=asc